E AX3073 1041-precondition-call.ax:24:4-14 undeclared-unsafe "`peek` calls `memGetWord`, whose safety depends on its caller, and its declaration does not say so" #"a precondition interface" !"`memGetWord` requires: `addr` names a live block of at least `index` + 1 words. A call to it is safe only when its caller makes that true, which is what `effect(unsafe)` here says this declaration does" ?23:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(unsafe)\n" ?"this fires where the unsafe operation is performed, not up the call chain. The tag alone makes the declaration a trusted encapsulation, whose callers inherit nothing; write `;@axiom:precondition(...)` beside it as well when its safety depends on what its caller passes. If the operation is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so"
E AX3073 1041-precondition-call.ax:28:4-13 undeclared-unsafe "`heading` calls `vecGetStr`, whose safety depends on its caller, and its declaration does not say so" #"a precondition interface" !"`vecGetStr` requires: the element at `i` holds a live `String`. A call to it is safe only when its caller makes that true, which is what `effect(unsafe)` here says this declaration does" ?27:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(unsafe)\n" ?"this fires where the unsafe operation is performed, not up the call chain. The tag alone makes the declaration a trusted encapsulation, whose callers inherit nothing; write `;@axiom:precondition(...)` beside it as well when its safety depends on what its caller passes. If the operation is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so"
E AX3073 1041-precondition-call.ax:38:4-10 undeclared-unsafe "`useLocal` calls `loadAt`, whose safety depends on its caller, and its declaration does not say so" #"a precondition interface" !"`loadAt` requires: `a` names a live word. A call to it is safe only when its caller makes that true, which is what `effect(unsafe)` here says this declaration does" ?37:1:"write `;@axiom:effect(unsafe)` above the declaration"~>";@axiom:effect(unsafe)\n" ?"this fires where the unsafe operation is performed, not up the call chain. The tag alone makes the declaration a trusted encapsulation, whose callers inherit nothing; write `;@axiom:precondition(...)` beside it as well when its safety depends on what its caller passes. If the operation is not wanted here the fix is to stop performing it, not to stop saying so"
E AX3010 1041-precondition-call.ax:42:6-10 axtag-mismatch "AXTAG mismatch on `pure`: `effect(pure)` claim contradicted: body performs Unsafe" ?"an AXTAG is a CLAIM, and this is the compiler answering it: make the body match the tag, or correct the tag to what the body does. Deleting the tag also silences this, and an untagged function is never checked - but that WITHDRAWS the claim rather than answering it, and every reader that trusted the tag loses the guarantee. A claim the walk cannot check is AX3037 and stays a warning; this code fires only where the walk has an answer"
